---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-5 pt-16 pb-12">
    <p class="text-mono-eyebrow font-mono text-cyan uppercase tracking-[0.18em]">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-heading-lg font-semibold text-ink">A small tool for moving files around.</h1>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-body-lg text-body">
      <p>Extract ZIP archives, preview common files, and create new archives without handing your files to a third party.</p>
      <p>While similar tools exist and are easy to build with modern AI assistants, this application is crafted with a deep focus on design and user experience. The aesthetic appeal isn't just for show—it's highly functional.</p>
      <p>The interface uses a deliberate palette of soft, muted greens and warm off-whites (like cream or beige). While looking at the color green doesn't magically fix or improve your eyesight, it is scientifically recognized as the most soothing color for the human eye to process. The human eye is most sensitive to the green spectrum, meaning it can process green light with the least amount of effort and stress on the eye muscles. Combined with warm off-whites, these choices dramatically reduce screen glare, lessen visual fatigue, and are scientifically considered the best background colors for minimizing digital eye strain.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>